# Website assets are served directly by GitHub Pages, which does not
# resolve Git LFS pointer files -- serving anything through LFS here
# produces broken images/audio/downloads on the live Pages URL even
# though the files look fine in the repo itself. Do not track jpg,
# jpeg, png, webp, svg, gif, mp3, wav, webm, pdf, docx or any other
# site asset with LFS. Keep all static assets as normal Git blobs so
# GitHub Pages serves them correctly.
#
# Scoped to actual binary types only -- a blanket "* -filter -diff
# -merge -text" here previously also disabled real diffs for every
# text file in the repo (html/json/js/css/py/md), so every PR ever
# merged in this project shows "Bin X -> Y bytes" instead of a
# reviewable line diff, for its entire history (verified against
# git show on several past commits). svg is real XML/text, so it
# keeps diffing normally -- it only opts out of the LFS filter.
*.jpg -filter -diff -merge -text
*.jpeg -filter -diff -merge -text
*.png -filter -diff -merge -text
*.webp -filter -diff -merge -text
*.gif -filter -diff -merge -text
*.mp3 -filter -diff -merge -text
*.wav -filter -diff -merge -text
*.webm -filter -diff -merge -text
*.pdf -filter -diff -merge -text
*.docx -filter -diff -merge -text
*.svg -filter
